---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'May 1, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Chord Sequence"
  description="Chord Sequence privacy policy. We don't collect personal data. Your chord progressions are stored in your browser's local storage — never on our servers."
  canonicalUrl="https://chordsequence.com/privacy/"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Home</a>
      <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg>
      <span class="text-foreground">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence does not collect personal data. There are no accounts, no sign-ups, and no tracking pixels.
          Your chord progressions are saved to your browser's local storage and never transmitted to any server.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">What data is stored — and where</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">When you use Chord Sequence, the app stores the following data <strong class="text-foreground">locally in your browser</strong> using the Web Storage API (<code class="text-primary text-sm">localStorage</code>):</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Names of your saved songs</li>
          <li>Chord sequences and BPM settings for each song</li>
          <li>App preferences (such as selected instrument sound)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This data lives entirely on your device. Clearing your browser's site data or storage will erase it.
          We have no access to this data and it is never sent to our servers.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">No accounts, no registration</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence does not offer user accounts. We do not collect names, email addresses, passwords, or any
          other personally identifying information.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">External requests</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">The app makes one external request for web fonts:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Google Fonts</strong> — to load the Inter, Lora, and Space Mono typefaces
            from <code class="text-primary text-sm">fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code class="text-primary text-sm">fonts.gstatic.com</code>.
            Google may log your IP address and browser type when these fonts are requested.
            This request does not set any tracking cookies and is not used for advertising.
            See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for details.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">No analytics scripts, advertising pixels, or third-party trackers are loaded by this site.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is hosted on Netlify. Netlify may collect standard server access logs (IP address, browser,
          pages visited, timestamp) as part of normal web hosting operations. This data is processed by Netlify under
          their own <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
          We do not access individual server logs for tracking or profiling purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence does not set any cookies. The app uses <code class="text-primary text-sm">localStorage</code>
          (not cookies) to persist your data between sessions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is a general-purpose music tool with no age restrictions. Because we collect no personal data,
          the app is safe for use by people of all ages. We do not knowingly collect information from children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we make changes to this privacy policy, we will update the effective date at the top of this page.
          Because we do not have your contact information, we cannot notify you directly — we recommend checking
          this page periodically if you have concerns.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this privacy policy? Reach us at <a href="/contact" class="text-primary hover:underline">our contact page</a> or by email at
          <a href="mailto:corsinoelias@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">corsinoelias@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
